whisper: Reading XML and HTML into parts. Written in Stellanova itself. Use it in a program with:  use: markup.stella
whisper: 'read markup text' gives the whole of it: a part with no name, holding the outermost parts.
whisper: HTML's loose ways are taken too: <br> and <img> need no closing, and a closing that doesn't fit ends the parts open inside it.

a markup part has:
  name (text)
  attributes (a table of text values)
  content (text)
  parts (a list of markup parts)
and the universe said i love you

a markup reader has:
  source (text)
  spot (a number)
and the universe said i love you

to plain markup, given words (text), returning text:
  set out to words
  set out to replace "&lt;" with "<" in out
  set out to replace "&gt;" with ">" in out
  set out to replace "&quot;" with a quotation mark in out
  set out to replace "&#39;" with "'" in out
  set out to replace "&apos;" with "'" in out
  set out to replace "&nbsp;" with " " in out
  set out to replace "&amp;" with "&" in out
  return out
and the universe said i love you

to upcoming, for a markup reader, given count (a number), returning text:
  set last to the size of source
  if spot exceeds last: return ""
  return letters spot to (smaller of (spot plus count minus 1) and last) of source
and the universe said i love you

to skip past, for a markup reader, given ending (text):
  set rest to upcoming with (the markup reader, the size of source)
  set n to position of ending in rest
  if n is 0:
    set spot to (the size of source) plus 1
  otherwise:
    set spot to spot plus n minus 1 plus the size of ending
and the universe said i love you

to name here, for a markup reader, returning text:
  set found to ""
  as long as spot is at most the size of source and not (letter spot of source is one of (" ", "/", ">", "=", new line)):
    set found to found plus letter spot of source
    set spot to spot plus 1
  return found
and the universe said i love you

to read element, for a markup reader, returning a markup part:
  conjure a markup part as part
  set the name of part to name here the markup reader
  set closed to no
  as long as spot is at most the size of source:
    set c to letter spot of source
    if c is ">":
      set spot to spot plus 1
      break free
    if c is one of (" ", "/", new line):
      if c is "/": set closed to yes
      set spot to spot plus 1
      move on
    set key to name here the markup reader
    set value to ""
    if upcoming with (the markup reader, 1) is "=":
      set spot to spot plus 1
      set mark to upcoming with (the markup reader, 1)
      if mark is one of (a quotation mark, "'"):
        set spot to spot plus 1
        as long as spot is at most the size of source and letter spot of source is not mark:
          set value to value plus letter spot of source
          set spot to spot plus 1
        set spot to spot plus 1
      otherwise:
        as long as spot is at most the size of source and not (letter spot of source is one of (" ", ">", new line)):
          set value to value plus letter spot of source
          set spot to spot plus 1
    if key is not "": set the entry key of the attributes of part to plain markup value
  set lower to lower case of the name of part
  if closed or lower is one of ("br", "img", "hr", "input", "meta", "link", "area", "base", "col", "embed", "source", "track", "wbr"):
    return part
  if lower is one of ("script", "style"):
    whisper: what's inside is kept as it is, up to its closing
    set rest to upcoming with (the markup reader, the size of source)
    set n to position of "</" plus the name of part in rest
    if n is 0: set n to (the size of rest) plus 1
    if n exceeds 1: set the content of part to letters 1 to (n minus 1) of rest
    set spot to spot plus n minus 1
    skip past with (the markup reader, ">")
    return part
  return read inside with (the markup reader, part)
and the universe said i love you

to read inside, for a markup reader, given part (a markup part), returning a markup part:
  set whole to part
  as long as spot is at most the size of source:
    if letter spot of source is not "<":
      set start to spot
      as long as spot is at most the size of source and letter spot of source is not "<":
        set spot to spot plus 1
      set the content of whole to the content of whole plus plain markup (letters start to (spot minus 1) of source)
    otherwise if upcoming with (the markup reader, 4) is "<!--":
      skip past with (the markup reader, "-->")
    otherwise if upcoming with (the markup reader, 2) is one of ("<!", "<?"):
      skip past with (the markup reader, ">")
    otherwise if upcoming with (the markup reader, 2) is "</":
      set back to spot
      set spot to spot plus 2
      set ending to name here the markup reader
      skip past with (the markup reader, ">")
      if lower case of ending is lower case of the name of whole: return whole
      if the name of whole is not "":
        whisper: it closes a part further out: this one ends here, and the one it closes reads it again
        set spot to back
        return whole
    otherwise:
      set spot to spot plus 1
      add read element the markup reader to the parts of whole
  return whole
and the universe said i love you

to read markup, given words (text), returning a markup part:
  conjure a markup reader as reader
  set the source of reader to words
  set the spot of reader to 1
  conjure a markup part as whole
  return read inside with (reader, whole)
and the universe said i love you

to parts named, given whole (a markup part) and wanted (text), returning a list of markup parts:
  set found to a list of markup parts
  for each p in the parts of whole:
    if lower case of the name of p is lower case of wanted: add p to found
    for each q in parts named with (p, wanted):
      add q to found
  return found
and the universe said i love you

to attribute, given part (a markup part) and key (text), returning text:
  if the attributes of part contains key: return the entry key of the attributes of part
  return ""
and the universe said i love you

to all words in, given whole (a markup part), returning text:
  whisper: the content of it and of every part inside, joined
  set out to the content of whole
  for each p in the parts of whole:
    set out to out plus all words in p
  return out
and the universe said i love you
